<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Templated from VFEP's VFEP_WarcasketHelmet_Siegebreaker (VFEPirates.WarcasketDef,
    ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketHelmetBase") at VFEP commit e237aba,
    1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Headgear.xml. Everything not listed under "Tuning" below,
    uiIconScale included, is still a verbatim Siegebreaker copy (placeholder, per TODOs.md).
    The apparel tags follow the armor's header.

    Tuning: costList ComponentSpacer 2 / Plasteel 70 (Siegebreaker 2 / 50, Guardian 2 / 70)
    follows the armor's 6 components / 180 plasteel at the helmet-to-armor ratios the 10th-gen
    sets use: components one third of the armor's (Siegebreaker, Guardian and Sarcophagus 2:6,
    Controller 4:12) and plasteel roughly 0.35 to 0.4 (Siegebreaker 50/145, Guardian 70/200,
    Controller 60/150, Sarcophagus 60/145; 180 x 0.35 to 0.4 is 63 to 72). Rounded up to the
    Guardian helmet's 70 rather than down to the 60 norm because this piece carries the
    Guardian helmet's plating plus a respirator and an aiming assist, so it must not also be
    the cheaper of the two at the foundry. ArmorRating_Blunt 1.5 is the Guardian helmet's value;
    see the armor's header for the set-wide close-combat plating rationale.

    Abilities, the sealed helm:
    - pawnCapacityMinLevels Breathing 1.0 through VEF's ApparelExtension: a built-in respirator,
      the Sarcophagus helmet's pattern for one capacity only.
    - equippedStatFactors AimingDelayFactor x0.95: a small ranged buff so the helmet earns its
      place without Odyssey (the set's melee lean sits on the shoulders). Kept small because the
      foundry lets any spacer armor take this helmet, and no VFEP helmet offers a ranged factor
      at all; VEF multiplies same-stat factors across worn pieces.
    - No jump-range contribution; see the armor's header.
    - Under Odyssey alone the set already totals VacuumResistance 1.0 (0.2 + 0.1 + 0.7). Under
      Vanilla Gravship Expanded the compat root lowers this piece to 0.65 (set 0.97) and gives
      it VGE1's oxygen-provider comp, so the helmet itself restores full immunity while its
      oxygen lasts, no astrorig or pack needed; see
      1.6/Mods/VanillaGravshipExpanded/Patches/HelmetOxygen.xml.
    - costList GravlitePanel 10 under Odyssey; see the armor's header for the split.

    SOS2/Universum parity: covered by our 1.6/Patches/SOS2Patch.xml alongside the armor (EVA tag
    + Insulation_Cold 100), mirroring what VFEP's own patch does for its helmets; see that
    file's header.

    Vanilla Gravship Expanded parity: our
    1.6/Mods/VanillaGravshipExpanded/Patches/VacuumResistance.xml lowers the 0.7 below to 0.65
    when VGE1 is active, the value VGE1 gives every VFEP spacer warcasket helmet; see the
    armor's header and that patch.

    Art: Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketShipcracker/WarcasketShipcrackerHelmet (+
    _north/_east/_south), 256x256 RGBA under the root Textures/ folder, mirroring VFEP's own
    warcasket layout.

    Draw order: no drawData override, not by lifting this piece's south offset over the
    pauldrons (that also raised it over every other set's pauldrons at the foundry); the
    ordering lives on the shoulders def instead (its header has the altitude derivation), which
    lowers our pauldrons under every helmet, so this helmet stays interchangeable with VFEP's.
  -->
  <VFEPirates.WarcasketDef ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketHelmetBase">
    <defName>SCWC_WarcasketHelmet_Shipcracker</defName>
    <label>shipcracker warcasket helmet</label>
    <shortDescription>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket helmet with improved impact dispersion, sealed and equipped with an onboard respirator and an aiming assist.</shortDescription>
    <description>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket helmet with improved impact dispersion, sealed and equipped with an onboard respirator and an aiming assist.\n\nAn Imperial pattern, not a pirate one: boarding corps built it on the 10th-generation spacer chassis to cross the gap between two ships and open the far hull from the outside. Salvage and desertion have since put it in foundries far from any Imperial dock.\n\nA shipcracker launches through the vacuum, lands on the enemy hull, punches through to the interior and takes the ship room by room. Under gravity the same burn clears a wall or a roof in a single hop. The shield stops bullets, not blades: pilots are chosen for a taste for close work.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketShipcracker/WarcasketShipcrackerHelmet</texPath>
    </graphicData>
    <uiIconScale>1.25</uiIconScale>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>8</Mass>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>2</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>1.5</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>1</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Insulation_Cold>5</Insulation_Cold>
      <Insulation_Heat>2</Insulation_Heat>
      <EquipDelay>1</EquipDelay>
    </statBases>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <PsychicSensitivity>-0.5</PsychicSensitivity>
      <ToxicResistance>0.5</ToxicResistance>
      <SlaveSuppressionOffset MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">0.1</SlaveSuppressionOffset>
      <VacuumResistance MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0.7</VacuumResistance>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <costList>
      <ComponentSpacer>2</ComponentSpacer>
      <Plasteel>70</Plasteel>
      <GravlitePanel MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">10</GravlitePanel>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <apparel>
      <bodyPartGroups>
        <li>FullHead</li>
      </bodyPartGroups>
      <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketShipcracker/WarcasketShipcrackerHelmet</wornGraphicPath>
      <layers>
        <li>Overhead</li>
      </layers>
      <tags>
        <!-- Reusing WarcasketVeteran puts this set on every Junker/Mercenary
             veteran-tier pawnkind (and Odyssey's salvager pawnkind); see
             TODOs.md open question.
        <li>WarcasketVeteran</li>
        -->
        <li>WarcasketAll</li>
      </tags>
    </apparel>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.ApparelExtension">
        <!-- priority: makes this entry the survivor when VEF merges it with the one
             VFEP_WarcasketHelmetBase carries; see the armor def's header. -->
        <priority>1</priority>
        <equippedStatFactors>
          <AimingDelayFactor>0.95</AimingDelayFactor>
        </equippedStatFactors>
        <pawnCapacityMinLevels>
          <li>
            <capacity>Breathing</capacity>
            <minLevel>1</minLevel>
          </li>
        </pawnCapacityMinLevels>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VFEPirates.WarcasketDef>
</Defs>
